    <h3>1. Introduction</h3>
    <p>Welcome to StudyShare, an academic learning platform designed to help students discover, access, and share educational resources.</p>
    <p>StudyShare provides features including academic notes, previous year question papers (PYQs), study materials, faculty profiles, doubt discussions, and other educational resources.</p>
    <p>This Privacy Policy explains how information may be collected, used, stored, and disclosed when you access or use our website.</p>
    <p>By using StudyShare, you acknowledge that you have read this Privacy Policy.</p>

    <h3>2. Information We Collect</h3>
    <p>Depending on how you use StudyShare, we may collect the following categories of information.</p>

    <h4>A. Account Information</h4>
    <p>When you register or use an account, we may collect:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Full name.</li>
      <li>Username.</li>
      <li>Email address.</li>
      <li>Profile photograph or avatar, if provided.</li>
      <li>Authentication information necessary to maintain your account.</li>
      <li>Account role, such as student, teacher, or administrator.</li>
    </ul>

    <h4>B. Academic Content</h4>
    <p>When you use our academic features, we may process:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Notes and study materials you upload.</li>
      <li>Previous year question papers and other academic resources.</li>
      <li>Questions and doubts you submit.</li>
      <li>Answers, comments, ratings, and feedback.</li>
      <li>Subject, semester, branch, and other academic information associated with your submissions.</li>
    </ul>

    <h4>C. Technical and Usage Information</h4>
    <p>When you access our website, technical information may be processed, including:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Browser and device information.</li>
      <li>IP address and connection information, where available.</li>
      <li>Pages visited and interactions with website features.</li>
      <li>Technical logs used to diagnose errors and protect the platform.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>If Google Analytics is enabled, certain website usage information may also be collected through analytics technologies.</p>

    <h3>3. How We Use Your Information</h3>
    <p>StudyShare may use information to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Create and maintain user accounts.</li>
      <li>Authenticate users and manage sessions.</li>
      <li>Provide access to student, teacher, and administrator features.</li>
      <li>Display and organize academic resources.</li>
      <li>Enable doubt discussions and academic collaboration.</li>
      <li>Process ratings, comments, and feedback.</li>
      <li>Manage uploaded files and educational content.</li>
      <li>Maintain platform security and prevent misuse.</li>
      <li>Diagnose technical problems and improve performance.</li>
      <li>Understand website traffic and user engagement.</li>
      <li>Comply with applicable legal obligations.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We use information for purposes relevant to operating and improving the platform.</p>

    <h3>4. Publicly Visible Information</h3>
    <p>Some information submitted to StudyShare may be visible to other users.</p>
    <p>For example, academic resources, questions, comments, and teacher profile information may be displayed according to the platform's features and access permissions.</p>
    <p>Users should avoid including sensitive personal information in publicly visible content.</p>
    <p>Account details and administrative information should only be accessible according to the platform's authorization rules.</p>

    <h3>5. Uploaded Files and Academic Resources</h3>
    <p>StudyShare allows eligible users to upload academic resources.</p>
    <p>Uploaded content may be stored using the file-storage infrastructure configured for the platform. Associated information, such as titles, subjects, and resource descriptions, may be stored separately.</p>
    <p>We may review, restrict, unpublish, or remove content that violates our policies or applicable law.</p>
    <p>Users should not upload documents containing private information belonging to themselves or other people unless they have an appropriate reason and authorization.</p>

    <h3>6. Cookies and Similar Technologies</h3>
    <p>StudyShare may use cookies and similar technologies to support:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Authentication and session management.</li>
      <li>Security-related functions.</li>
      <li>Website preferences and functionality.</li>
      <li>Analytics and website performance measurement.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Where Google Analytics is enabled, it may use cookies or similar technologies to measure website interactions.</p>
    <p>For more information, please read our Cookie Policy.</p>

    <h3>7. Sharing of Information</h3>
    <p>We do not make users' private account information publicly available merely because they register on StudyShare.</p>
    <p>Information may be processed or disclosed when reasonably necessary for:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Hosting and operating the website.</li>
      <li>Database and file storage.</li>
      <li>Authentication and security.</li>
      <li>Analytics and performance monitoring.</li>
      <li>Responding to lawful requests.</li>
      <li>Protecting the rights, security, and integrity of StudyShare and its users.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Third-party service providers may process information according to their respective terms and privacy policies.</p>

    <h3>8. Data Security</h3>
    <p>We use technical and organizational measures intended to protect information against unauthorized access, misuse, alteration, or loss.</p>
    <p>These measures may include authentication, access controls, session management, and server-side authorization.</p>
    <p>However, no website or electronic storage system can guarantee absolute security.</p>
    <p>Users should keep their credentials confidential and notify us if they suspect unauthorized access to their accounts.</p>

    <h3>9. Data Retention</h3>
    <p>We retain information for as long as reasonably necessary to provide the platform, maintain accounts, meet operational requirements, resolve disputes, and comply with applicable legal obligations.</p>
    <p>Retention periods may vary depending on the type of information and its purpose.</p>
    <p>Information may be retained in backups or technical records for a limited period where necessary.</p>

    <h3>10. Your Privacy Rights</h3>
    <p>Depending on applicable law, you may have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Request access to your personal information.</li>
      <li>Request correction of inaccurate information.</li>
      <li>Request deletion of eligible personal information.</li>
      <li>Withdraw consent where processing relies on consent.</li>
      <li>Raise concerns about how your information is handled.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Some information may need to be retained where required by law or necessary for legitimate operational purposes.</p>

    <h3>11. Children's Privacy</h3>
    <p>StudyShare is intended for users who can lawfully use the platform under applicable age requirements.</p>
    <p>We do not knowingly seek to collect personal information from children in violation of applicable law.</p>
    <p>If you believe a child has provided personal information inappropriately, please contact us.</p>

    <h3>12. Third-Party Websites</h3>
    <p>StudyShare may contain links to external websites and services.</p>
    <p>We do not control the privacy practices of those external services. Users should review their respective privacy policies before providing information.</p>

    <h3>13. Changes to This Policy</h3>
    <p>We may update this Privacy Policy to reflect changes in our features, operations, or legal obligations.</p>
    <p>Updates will be published on this page with a revised date.</p>

